0 then … else …` so that both branches are literally present. Do not. Every downstream obligation is then stated over the `if`-form — including BOTH `IntegrableOn` hypotheses of the split — so each branch-free half-line lemma costs a `setIntegral_congr_fun` and each integrability fact an `IntegrableOn.congr_fun`, and what is left over is a bare `congr 1` that reports as a shape mismatch rather than as a mathematical gap. Split the ORIGINAL integrand and remove the branch on each piece AFTERWARDS, where the membership hypothesis is in scope and `abs_of_pos` / `abs_of_nonpos` discharge it in one rewrite; state every half-line helper lemma over that same original integrand rather than over its simplified branch. If you genuinely need a branchy global function, build it with `Set.piecewise`, not a raw `if`: `MeasureTheory.integral_piecewise` splits it in one step and takes its integrability hypotheses on the two branch-free pieces.", :hx/id "hx-mem-1aa18a67-adf3-4262-8070-e44dc1744e3f", :hx/ends [{:entity-id "e-1aa18a67-adf3-4262-8070-e44dc1744e3f"} {:entity-id "a97J06"} {:entity-id "math-formalization-CA/measure-integration-api"} {:entity-id "apm-role-6c5c056af7d2b0ccb4e8011c0968decced3d69d036cd53de9548cfd6be619853"}], :prop/roles {:entry "e-1aa18a67-adf3-4262-8070-e44dc1744e3f", :subjects ["a97J06" "math-formalization-CA/measure-integration-api"], :distills [], :session "apm-role-6c5c056af7d2b0ccb4e8011c0968decced3d69d036cd53de9548cfd6be619853", :patterns ["math-formalization-CA/measure-integration-api"]}, :prop/name "split-the-original-integrand-never-manufacture-an-if-to-fit-the-split", :hx/props {:hook "Splitting a measure-theoretic integral over the line into two half-lines when the integrand is only PIECEWISE equal to the forms your evaluation lemmas want — an `|x|`, a sign, a two-sided decay. Both split lemmas (`intervalIntegral.integral_Iic_add_Ioi`, `MeasureTheory.integral_add_compl`) take ONE global function, so it is tempting to redefine the integrand as `if x ∈ Ioi 0 then … else …` so that both branches are literally present. Do not. Every downstream obligation is then stated over the `if`-form — including BOTH `IntegrableOn` hypotheses of the split — so each branch-free half-line lemma costs a `setIntegral_congr_fun` and each integrability fact an `IntegrableOn.congr_fun`, and what is left over is a bare `congr 1` that reports as a shape mismatch rather than as a mathematical gap. Split the ORIGINAL integrand and remove the branch on each piece AFTERWARDS, where the membership hypothesis is in scope and `abs_of_pos` / `abs_of_nonpos` discharge it in one rewrite; state every half-line helper lemma over that same original integrand rather than over its simplified branch. If you genuinely need a branchy global function, build it with `Set.piecewise`, not a raw `if`: `MeasureTheory.integral_piecewise` splits it in one step and takes its integrability hypotheses on the two branch-free pieces.", :volatile? false, :name "split-the-original-integrand-never-manufacture-an-if-to-fit-the-split", :roles {:entry "e-1aa18a67-adf3-4262-8070-e44dc1744e3f", :subjects ["a97J06" "math-formalization-CA/measure-integration-api"], :distills [], :session "apm-role-6c5c056af7d2b0ccb4e8011c0968decced3d69d036cd53de9548cfd6be619853", :patterns ["math-formalization-CA/measure-integration-api"]}, :state :current, :review {:evidence-id "e-apm-promotion-review-19bd7db0da4e3b9c8dceb0ea0e66ffdf", :reviewer "f41-promotion-proctor", :session-id "apm-role-b49398131462bb3a3f348497daea030a0f1033c3da1fe0fd4eb6054dd9f9f9e6", :verdict :approve, :pattern-ids ["math-formalization-CA/measure-integration-api"], :reviewed-at "2026-08-26T10:01:25.290918934Z"}, :attachment-status :reviewed, :kind :reference, :review-history [{:evidence-id "e-apm-promotion-review-19bd7db0da4e3b9c8dceb0ea0e66ffdf", :reviewer "f41-promotion-proctor", :session-id "apm-role-b49398131462bb3a3f348497daea030a0f1033c3da1fe0fd4eb6054dd9f9f9e6", :verdict :approve, :pattern-ids ["math-formali