on is then this, not a combinatorial pairing argument.", :hx/id "hx-mem-6556333d-b0d0-4e5a-802b-15b7d452553a", :hx/ends [{:entity-id "e-6556333d-b0d0-4e5a-802b-15b7d452553a"} {:entity-id "a97A01"} {:entity-id "apm-role-c1f735418a24b1cca1e404cb56ab5cb09e45bea8ffda2121f09b2b134a8467f8"} {:entity-id "math-formalization-CA/measure-integration-api"}], :prop/roles {:entry "e-6556333d-b0d0-4e5a-802b-15b7d452553a", :subjects ["a97A01" "math-formalization-CA/measure-integration-api"], :distills [], :session "apm-role-c1f735418a24b1cca1e404cb56ab5cb09e45bea8ffda2121f09b2b134a8467f8", :patterns ["math-formalization-CA/measure-integration-api"]}, :prop/name "pair-cancellation-is-an-induction-not-a-bijection", :hx/props {:hook "Cancelling alternating contributions over a decomposition: do not build an explicit pairing bijection on the index Finset. If the terms cancel in consecutive pairs, sum over `Finset.range (2 * k)` and induct on k, peeling TWO terms per step with `Finset.sum_range_succ` twice; the pair hypothesis `forall i, g (2*i) + g (2*i+1) = 0` then closes each step by `simpa using h k`, with `2 * (k+1) = (2*k+1) + 1` supplied by `ring` before the rewrite. Whole proof is six lines and needs no reindexing lemma, no `Finset.sum_nbij`, no even/odd filter split. Verified: elaborates against the pinned Mathlib, exit 0, no sorry. Use it whenever a signed function is constant on each cell of a refinement and adjacent cells carry opposite signs — the sum-side obligation is then this, not a combinatorial pairing argument.", :volatile? false, :name "pair-cancellation-is-an-induction-not-a-bijection", :roles {:entry "e-6556333d-b0d0-4e5a-802b-15b7d452553a", :subjects ["a97A01" "math-formalization-CA/measure-integration-api"], :distills [], :session "apm-role-c1f735418a24b1cca1e404cb56ab5cb09e45bea8ffda2121f09b2b134a8467f8", :patterns ["math-formalization-CA/measure-integration-api"]}, :state :current, :review {:evidence-id "e-apm-promotion-review-1917562ea8bec8ec33ed4b88a7341068"