gainst `-↑s` inside `Complex.exp`, so that `congr 1` on the exponential's argument does not close. Two rules. Normalize casts on BOTH sides at once (`push_cast at h ⊢`): `Complex.ofReal_neg`/`ofReal_inv`/`ofReal_div`/`ofReal_mul`/`ofReal_exp` are all `@[simp, norm_cast]`, and pushing only the side you are looking at is what manufactures the mismatch. And clear the constant by proving the single scalar identity `((c : ℝ) : ℂ) * ((c⁻¹ : ℝ) : ℂ) = 1` as a standalone `have` — `push_cast`, then `field_simp` under the nonvanishing fact lifted by `exact_mod_cast Real.pi_ne_zero` — then rewriting the equation with it, rather than running a field-clearing tactic on an equation one of whose atoms is an integral.", :hx/id "hx-mem-bd971ae9-6833-4e83-99a4-c0a2e0abe47e", :hx/ends [{:entity-id "e-bd971ae9-6833-4e83-99a4-c0a2e0abe47e"} {:entity-id "a97J06"} {:entity-id "math-formalization/cast-normalization"} {:entity-id "apm-role-0ab6967207acf7e015b61c3da0fe892f063968c853d82e1e3ee637e41bfa7c6a"}], :prop/roles {:entry "e-bd971ae9-6833-4e83-99a4-c0a2e0abe47e", :subjects ["a97J06" "math-formalization/cast-normalization"], :distills [], :session "apm-role-0ab6967207acf7e015b61c3da0fe892f063968c853d82e1e3ee637e41bfa7c6a", :patterns ["math-formalization/cast-normalization"]}, :prop/name "clear-a-transform-normalizing-constant-in-the-scalars-only", :hx/props {:hook "A transform-convention normalizing constant (`1/π`, `1/(2*π)`, `1/√(2*π)`) is left multiplying a COMPLEX-valued integral and has to be cleared before the answer can be read off, and `field_simp`/`ring` on the whole equation keeps failing on cast mismatches — typically a cast of a compound such as `↑(-s)` sitting against `-↑s` inside `Complex.exp`, so that `congr 1` on the exponential's argument does not close. Two rules. Normalize casts on BOTH sides at once (`push_cast at h ⊢`): `Complex.ofReal_neg`/`ofReal_inv`/`ofReal_div`/`ofReal_mul`/`ofReal_exp` are all `@[simp, norm_cast]`, and pushing only the side you are looking at 